5. Summary of findings
A student system works best when it is small, uses one tool for tasks and one for notes, and has a fixed weekly review. PARA handles task organization; Zettelkasten handles learning. AI helps most with summarizing, quiz creation and weekly review drafts, and must be checked for errors.
6. Limitations
Findings are based on published method descriptions and tool documentation. The student's own 2-week trial data is needed to judge whether the system is actually used.
